  "question": {
    "text": "A curve is such that the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-intercept of the tangent drawn to it at the point <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is reciprocal of the abscissa of <math><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then, the equation of the curve is (where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is the constant of integration and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)"
  },
